WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.067 --> 00:00:18.957
Not long after I had returned to England, my family and I said our good-byes again.

2
00:00:18.958 --> 00:00:25.668
On June 20, 1702, I left England on a ship called the Adventure.

3
00:00:25.669 --> 00:00:30.313
It was going to sail around Africa to India.

4
00:00:30.314 --> 00:00:35.479
The winds were good on the way to the Cape of Good Hope in southern Africa.

5
00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:39.201
When we arrived in the harbor, the captain said,

6
00:00:39.202 --> 00:00:41.637
"We'll stay here until March."

7
00:00:41.638 --> 00:00:44.553
"But why?" I asked.

8
00:00:44.554 --> 00:00:48.151
"The ship needs some repairs," he explained.

9
00:00:48.152 --> 00:00:51.350
"And the winds are not good now for sailing to India.

10
00:00:51.351 --> 00:00:53.447
The March winds will be better."

11
00:00:53.448 --> 00:00:56.455
"I'm not pleased," I said.

12
00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:58.803
"I want to see India."

13
00:00:58.804 --> 00:01:02.433
"Can't you explore this place?" said the captain.

14
00:01:02.434 --> 00:01:04.866
"There is much to see here."

15
00:01:04.867 --> 00:01:06.884
The captain was right.

16
00:01:06.885 --> 00:01:12.315
In Africa I met fascinating people and saw some amazing animals.

17
00:01:12.316 --> 00:01:15.972
But I was impatient to continue our trip.

18
00:01:15.973 --> 00:01:22.085
Finally, in March of 1703, the Adventure set sail for India.

19
00:01:22.086 --> 00:01:29.151
The winds were good until we got near Madagascar, an island off the east coast of Africa.

20
00:01:29.152 --> 00:01:32.176
Then a strong wind began to blow.

21
00:01:32.177 --> 00:01:37.672
The sea was very rough and tossed our little ship around for twenty days.

22
00:01:37.673 --> 00:01:41.032
Then, suddenly, the wind stopped.

23
00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:44.499
"This perfect calm is very pleasant,"

24
00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:49.416
I said to the captain, who had sailed the oceans for many years.

25
00:01:49.417 --> 00:01:53.780
"It won't last long," he replied with a worried look.

26
00:01:53.781 --> 00:01:56.961
"I think a bad storm will begin soon."

27
00:01:56.962 --> 00:02:01.817
To the crew he shouted, "Prepare for rough seas tomorrow!"

28
00:02:01.818 --> 00:02:08.406
As the captain had predicted, the next day the wind got stronger and stronger.

29
00:02:08.407 --> 00:02:12.483
The crew adjusted the sails as the violent storm raged.

30
00:02:12.484 --> 00:02:16.871
The fierce wind howled and the waves broke over the ship.

31
00:02:16.872 --> 00:02:23.272
After many hours, the wind finally became less violent and the sea became calmer.

32
00:02:23.273 --> 00:02:28.173
The storm had blown the Adventure hundreds of kilometers to the east.

33
00:02:28.174 --> 00:02:31.922
"Where are we?" I asked the captain.

34
00:02:31.923 --> 00:02:38.344
"I can't tell for sure," he said, "but our supply of water is now very low.

35
00:02:38.345 --> 00:02:42.184
We must reach land soon and fill our water barrels."

36
00:02:42.185 --> 00:02:46.244
Many days passed and we saw nothing but the sea.

37
00:02:46.245 --> 00:02:51.417
At last, one morning a sailor cried out, "Land!"

38
00:02:51.418 --> 00:02:54.740
Everyone on the ship was happy to hear that word.

39
00:02:54.741 --> 00:02:57.255
The ship sailed closer to the land.

40
00:02:57.256 --> 00:03:01.912
We could not tell whether it was a large island or a continent.

41
00:03:01.913 --> 00:03:07.834
"You men," said the captain to some of the crew, "take the rowboats and go ashore.

42
00:03:07.835 --> 00:03:10.711
Fill the water barrels with fresh water."

43
00:03:10.712 --> 00:03:15.502
"Captain," I said, "may I go with them to take a look at this place?"

44
00:03:15.503 --> 00:03:17.932
"Of course," he replied.

45
00:03:17.933 --> 00:03:20.504
"You can tell me later what it is like."

46
00:03:20.505 --> 00:03:25.032
When the rowboats reached the shore, one of the sailors said,

47
00:03:25.033 --> 00:03:28.224
"I see no rivers or streams nearby.

48
00:03:28.225 --> 00:03:32.514
We will have to walk along the shore to look for fresh water."

49
00:03:32.515 --> 00:03:36.962
"I'm going to walk inland to explore a little," I told them.

50
00:03:36.963 --> 00:03:39.677
"I will meet you back here in an hour."

51
00:03:39.678 --> 00:03:43.819
I walked about a kilometer, enjoying being on land again.

52
00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:47.559
Then I turned and walked back to meet the crew.

53
00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:51.654
When I arrived on the beach, the sailors were not there.

54
00:03:51.655 --> 00:03:56.704
They were in the rowboats, rowing as fast as they could toward the Adventure.

55
00:03:56.705 --> 00:04:02.863
I was going to shout out to them, when I saw a huge giant walking through the sea.

56
00:04:02.864 --> 00:04:05.758
It was trying to catch up with the rowboats.

57
00:04:05.759 --> 00:04:11.904
The sailors were almost at the ship, and I could see that the giant would not catch them.

58
00:04:11.905 --> 00:04:14.919
I did not wait to see what happened next.

59
00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:20.185
I ran as fast as I could in the other direction.
